WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.714
Scenario: Alerts show file encryption, unusual service-account use and unusual

2
00:00:05.714 --> 00:00:11.429
outbound traffic. The initial access path is unknown. Safest response:

3
00:00:11.429 --> 00:00:17.143
activate the incident plan, isolate confirmed affected assets, preserve evidence

4
00:00:17.143 --> 00:00:22.857
and scope related hosts and accounts. Option B is unsafe

5
00:00:22.857 --> 00:00:28.571
because A blanket shutdown can destroy volatile evidence and disrupt

6
00:00:28.571 --> 00:00:34.286
unaffected services. Option C is unsafe because Waiting for attribution

7
00:00:34.286 --> 00:00:40.000
can allow active damage to continue. Option D is unsafe

8
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:45.714
because Direct uncoordinated contact bypasses the authorized response structure. In

9
00:00:45.714 --> 00:00:51.429
practice: appoint an incident lead, preserve logs, contain proportionately and

10
00:00:51.429 --> 00:00:57.143
record decisions and unknowns. Key takeaway: respond to credible indicators

11
00:00:57.143 --> 00:01:00.000
without waiting for perfect attribution.

